#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""eesel — a simple CLI for the eesel.ai platform.

Auth model:
  * `eesel login`           opens dashboard.eesel.ai in your browser, the
                            page sends the workspace JWT back to a local
                            HTTP server we spin up briefly. Standard CLI
                            OAuth bridge pattern.
  * `eesel login --dev`     mints a local JWT against the dev secret and
                            auto-discovers workspace/agent IDs from your
                            local Postgres container (no browser needed).
  * `eesel link <url>`      points one git worktree at a branch (preprod) env:
                            writes a gitignored eesel.dev.json holding just the
                            URL, and every command there mints a throwaway token
                            from that env's /dev/session per run (no token on
                            disk). Discovered by walking up from cwd like `.git`.

Sessions: stored at ~/.config/eesel/sessions/<id>.json; each maps to one
ongoing chat with a stable taskId + message history. `current.json` tracks
which session is "active" so plain `eesel chat "msg"` knows where to send.

API surface used:
  POST /workspaces/token             (dashboard side, prod login bridge only)
  GET  /agents                       list agents in the workspace (each row
                                       already includes the agent's `prompt`,
                                       which `eesel instructions` prints)
  GET  /triggers/registry            list available trigger types/keys
                                       (eesel automations triggers registry)
  GET  /agents/{id}/triggers         list triggers configured for one agent.
                                       The CLI splits these by trigger_key:
                                       event/webhook triggers → `eesel automations
                                       triggers list` (grouped by integration);
                                       scheduled jobs → `eesel automations
                                       schedules list`
  POST /agents/{id}/triggers         add a trigger to an agent (eesel automations
                                       triggers add) or a scheduled job (eesel
                                       automations schedules add, sends
                                       trigger_key=eesel_scheduled)
  DELETE /triggers/{id}              remove a trigger / scheduled job (eesel
                                       automations triggers remove / schedules remove)
  GET  /agents/{id}/tools            list an agent's actions
                                       (eesel integrations <integration> actions)
  GET  /integrations                 list workspace integrations + connection
                                       status (eesel integrations)
  GET  /integration-definitions      the connectable catalog: each type's
                                       connection_options (eesel integrations
                                       available; drives eesel integrations connect)
  POST /integrations/{key}/{option}  connect via a "submit" connection option,
                                       e.g. /integrations/zendesk/quick_start
                                       (eesel integrations connect --option)
  POST /integrations/{id}/trigger-sync  trigger a data sync (eesel integrations sync)
  GET  /v2/sync-runs                 sync-run status + progress (eesel integrations
                                       sync-status; also the sync field of `show`)
  POST /agents/sandbox/start         start/continue a chat, returns {taskId,streamUrl}
                                       optional triggerId → preview a scheduled
                                       job's context in chat
  GET  /agents/chat/{id}/raw-stream  SSE stream of UI message chunks
  POST /triggers/{id}/fire           manually fire a scheduled job
                                       (eesel automations schedules fire)
  POST /workspace/tasks              list/count workspace tasks (agent activity)
  GET  /workspace/tasks/{id}/history full transcript of one task, grouped by run
  POST /workspace/tasks/analytics    aggregated task analytics (resolution, CSAT)
  POST /tasks/export                 start a CSV export of tasks (link emailed)
"""

